I finally ascended a Necromancer in Slash'em!

After doing pretty well in this years Nethack Tournament, and getting
the Double Top, I decided to try something I hadn't ever been able to
do before, ascending a Necromancer in Slash'em.  I've ascended a few
other characters in Slash'em, mostly Wizards, but for some reason, I
found the Necromancer really hard to ascend.

I picked a Doppleganger Necromancer, and had a really good game, after
my 4 tournament Nethack ascensions, I was being pretty careful, but
didn't find any early wishes to help.  Eventually got to the castle,
and got the wand of wishing there, but by that time, I had got some
wishes from Gypsies.

Carried around a wide selection of weapons:

 a - the rustproof +2 Deep Freeze
 b - the fireproof +6 Bat from Hell (weapon in hand)
 q - the cursed rustproof +0 Grimtooth
 t - the rustproof +0 Serpent's Tongue
 x - the blessed rustproof +7 Stormbringer
 G - the +6 Great Dagger of Glaurgnaa
 K - the +4 Skullcrusher

Sure like that energy recharge of the Great Dagger of Glaurgnaa.  My
main weapon was the Bat from Hell, that +5 to hit and +20 damage was
really sweet.

The Hand of Vecna, with it's hungerless regeneration was very useful,
and before I accidentally sacrificed the Eye of the Beholder, my
character enjoyed #invoking it and watching everything scream in agony.

Had an accident at the castle where I fell in the moat, which is Lethe
in this version, and my nice magic candle turned into a tallow candle,
so I got the magic lamp from the Sunless Sea.

I used the thoroughly rusty thoroughly corroded Key of Chaos as my key,
so nice to have something that doesn't ever break.

One of the best things about Necromancers is that they are immune to
sickness, that helped me many times.

